WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:03.750
The Plague Doctor had seen a great deal of
death in his time.

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:07.410
It was the very nature of the work he devoted
his life to.

00:00:07.410 --> 00:00:12.349
Patients were lost on the operating table
or taken from him, soldiers fell on the battlefield

00:00:12.349 --> 00:00:17.080
right before his eyes, even the simple touch
of his hand could stop a person's heart.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:22.840
He had watched the world outside turn to hell
as the sun destroyed every living thing that

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:25.410
wandered into its beams of accursed light.

00:00:25.410 --> 00:00:31.439
But somehow, even after all that he had witnessed,
this latest loss weighed heavy on his heart.

00:00:31.439 --> 00:00:36.400
He hadn't known Fernand well, or worked with
him for very long, but he had offered comfort

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.770
and support in a time when all seemed lost.

00:00:39.770 --> 00:00:44.750
The giant man had been steadfast, loyal, and
dedicated to the cause.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:48.160
So devoted, in fact, that he gave his very
life for it.

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.239
It was Fernand's choice to go that way, to
roll the dice and risk his body for the sake

00:00:53.239 --> 00:00:54.660
of the Doctor's work.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:59.899
He knew that, and yet...the pain pressed down
on him like a dark ocean, uncharted waters

00:00:59.899 --> 00:01:03.490
that threatened to drown the Doctor in a grief
he had never felt before.

00:01:03.490 --> 00:01:08.450
He knew that the work was waiting, he could
hear the cries of the fleshy creatures oozing

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:12.170
by outside, waiting to be cured of their ailment.

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:16.470
Still, he could not pull himself out from
beneath the blanket of deep depression that

00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.930
weighed him down.

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:23.630
All day, he would lie in his bed, a cot formerly
reserved for D-Class prisoners, staring up

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:26.800
at the ceiling and feeling the minutes tick
by.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:32.490
Eventually it all began to blur together,
with no need to eat, drink, or even sleep,

00:01:32.490 --> 00:01:35.750
there was nothing to break up the passage
of time.

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:36.750
"Doctor?"

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:41.020
The Plague Doctor lifted his head for the
first time in a long time at the sound of

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:43.140
a voice coming from the doorway.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:46.750
There stood Lord Blackwood, the dapper gentleman
sea slug.

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:50.189
His rhinophores twitched curiously as he slithered
into the room.

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:51.890
"Hello my friend..."

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:52.890
The Doctor sighed.

00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:55.710
"I say, I've been a bit worried about you
old chap!"

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:56.850
Lord Blackwood said.

00:01:56.850 --> 00:01:59.320
"We haven't seen you in quite some time!

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:02.010
Not since the untimely loss of our dear comrade
Fernand."

00:02:02.010 --> 00:02:05.250
"I confess I am finding it hard to carry on.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.399
Does it not seem hopeless?

00:02:07.399 --> 00:02:10.200
To continue the fight against the forces out
there?

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:14.700
How could I be so arrogant, to think I could
do battle with the sun itself?"

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:17.920
The Plague Doctor rested his head in his gloved
hands.

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:18.930
"Balderdash!"

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.090
Lord Blackwood shouted.

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.209
The Doctor looked up at him, startled.

00:02:22.209 --> 00:02:26.420
"Forgive my outburst, old sport, but that
is the grief speaking through you.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:31.730
As intelligent men we must honor our feelings,
as they are parts of us, but they cannot be

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:32.730
our rulers!

00:02:32.730 --> 00:02:37.360
As the great poet William Ernest Henley once
wrote: 'It matters not how strait the gate,

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:43.030
how charged with punishments the scroll, I
am the master of my fate, I am the captain

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.030
of my soul.'"

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:46.360
"Stirring words, and yet..."

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:47.620
The Doctor trailed off.

00:02:47.620 --> 00:02:48.860
"And yet what?!"

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:50.800
Lord Blackwood seemed to swell with emotion.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:57.110
"We find ourselves in dire times, yes, but
what are we to do in the face of them?

00:02:57.110 --> 00:02:59.379
Roll over, show our bellies, and embrace defeat?

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:01.300
Not I, sir!

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:04.560
Never I. I don't believe you should either.

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.830
Would Fernand have wanted you to let yourself
be lost this way?"

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.560
The Plague Doctor sat with that thought for
a moment.

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.709
Then, solemnly, he shook his head.

00:03:12.709 --> 00:03:14.140
"No, he wouldn't."

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:15.849
"Then we shall rally!

00:03:15.849 --> 00:03:19.670
Pick yourself up, come with me, and in the
memory of our fallen friend we will sing a

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:21.950
happy tune, as he would have!

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:27.230
We mourn, we celebrate his life, and then,
as we always have, we do what needs to be

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:28.230
done!

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:29.440
Come with me, Doctor."

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:34.700
The sea slug led the way, and, though he still
felt the call of the void tugging at his heels,

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:35.820
the Doctor Followed.

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:40.170
Dimly, he could hear Lord Blackwood ask, "Are
you familiar with the works of Gilbert and

00:03:40.170 --> 00:03:41.170
Sullivan?"

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:45.560
The Plague Doctor was not, in fact, familiar
with them, so he could not join in as Lord

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:50.590
Blackwood attempted to lead him in a chorus
of "I am the very model of a modern Major-General."

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:56.290
Still, the sound of music, of any kind of
joyful noise, lifted his spirits just the

00:03:56.290 --> 00:03:57.290
same.

00:03:57.290 --> 00:04:01.670
The two spent several hours together, swapping
old stories, singing songs, and remembering

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:03.620
Fernand, the lovable cannibal.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:08.370
At one point, Lord Blackwood brought out a
tankard of home-brewed ale he had been working

00:04:08.370 --> 00:04:10.980
on in one of the empty laboratories.

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:15.580
It smelled strange, and tasted stranger, but
it was still nice to share a drink with a

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.010
companion after so much hardship.

00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:22.699
Eventually, Lord Blackwood passed out, flopped
over on his side and snoring softly.

00:04:22.699 --> 00:04:28.410
The Doctor leaned against a wall nearby, resting
his eyes for the first time in many, many

00:04:28.410 --> 00:04:29.410
days.

00:04:29.410 --> 00:04:34.430
It wasn't happiness, not quite, but it was
a kind of peace, and a welcome reprieve from

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:37.050
the torturous thoughts that had gripped him
as of late.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:42.259
But the peace did not last, as the Doctor
began to hear sounds from within the tunnel,

00:04:42.259 --> 00:04:46.030
the passage that led somewhere deep beneath
the Foundation Site.

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:49.340
He could hear footsteps, muffled voices, creeping
ever closer.

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:53.960
They did not sound like the fleshy monster
who had invaded the facility before, but he

00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:56.620
could not be certain if they were friend or
foe.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:59.840
He scrambled to his feet, prepared to defend
himself if necessary.

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:00.920
"Lord Blackwood!"

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:06.070
He hissed, attempting to rouse his sleeping
friend, but the slug continued to snooze away.

00:05:06.070 --> 00:05:10.060
If the need to retreat arose, he would have
to use something to scoop up the sleeping

00:05:10.060 --> 00:05:12.039
slug and carry him to safety.

00:05:12.039 --> 00:05:16.850
The Plague Doctor was just picking up a nearby
bucket when the first of his unexpected visitors

00:05:16.850 --> 00:05:18.620
emerged from the darkness.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:23.810
It appeared to be an ordinary human man, wrapped
in dark robes that covered his face.

00:05:23.810 --> 00:05:26.650
His arms were left bare, and glinted in the
low light.

00:05:26.650 --> 00:05:31.300
They appeared to be made of metal, though
the Doctor did not recognize the kind.

00:05:31.300 --> 00:05:36.990
He removed his robes to reveal a deeply tanned
face, black hair, and piercing blue eyes.

00:05:36.990 --> 00:05:42.000
There was an arcane symbol carved into the
man's forehead, just above the gaze that now

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.740
fell on the Plague Doctor.

00:05:43.740 --> 00:05:48.380
A beat of silence passed between the two men,
before the Doctor finally spoke up.

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.540
"Please, sir, identify yourself."

00:05:50.540 --> 00:05:55.009
The strange man stared at him curiously, not
quite knowing what to make of him.

00:05:55.009 --> 00:05:56.150
"My name is Cain.

00:05:56.150 --> 00:05:57.610
And who are you?"

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:58.610
He asked.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:01.150
"I am a doctor," He answered simply.

00:06:01.150 --> 00:06:03.250
"How did you find this place?"

00:06:03.250 --> 00:06:04.400
"I had some help..."

00:06:04.400 --> 00:06:09.690
At this, Cain glanced over his shoulder, to
unseen companions waiting in the shadows.

00:06:09.690 --> 00:06:10.690
"It's safe here!

00:06:10.690 --> 00:06:11.810
You can come out!"

00:06:11.810 --> 00:06:15.169
As the Plague Doctor watched, three more figures
emerged from the tunnel.

00:06:15.169 --> 00:06:18.620
First, a man wearing a kind of light-blocking
HazMat suit.

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:23.520
He removed the suit slowly, exposing blond
hair, green eyes, a tattered brightly-colored

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:25.560
t-shirt, and cargo shorts.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:29.060
The man that followed just behind him was
wearing a similar suit, and removed it to

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:33.449
reveal a lab coat and an unusual necklace
hanging around his neck.

00:06:33.449 --> 00:06:37.349
The final visitor was not a man at all, but
a large mass of slime.

00:06:37.349 --> 00:06:42.430
At first, the Plague Doctor felt a shock of
anxiety, but at a second glance, he recognized

00:06:42.430 --> 00:06:43.849
the slimy creature.

00:06:43.849 --> 00:06:49.639
It was SCP-999, the friendly being that often
roamed the halls of this very site!

00:06:49.639 --> 00:06:51.720
It cooed excitedly at the sight of the Doctor.

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:57.240
Though it knew not to touch him, its pseudopods
wiggled in a gesture resembling a wave "hello."

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.220
"Yes, hello, my friend!"

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:02.509
The Plague Doctor smiled "But who are the
rest of you?"

00:07:02.509 --> 00:07:05.320
His eyes settled again on the amulet around
the third man's neck.

00:07:05.320 --> 00:07:07.250
He had seen it somewhere before...

00:07:07.250 --> 00:07:08.250
"Ah!

00:07:08.250 --> 00:07:09.800
Dr. Bright, I presume?

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:12.680
I'm afraid I did not recognize you with this
new face."

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:13.950
Dr. Bright grinned broadly.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:14.950
"Yep!

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:15.950
It's me!

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:17.620
A little apocalypse can't keep Dr. Bright
down.

00:07:17.620 --> 00:07:19.539
Good to see you again, Doctor.

00:07:19.539 --> 00:07:20.819
This is SCP-507."

00:07:20.819 --> 00:07:23.100
He gestured to the blond man.

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.770
"You can call me Guy."

00:07:24.770 --> 00:07:27.349
He stuck out his hand to shake, but the Doctor
shook his head.

00:07:27.349 --> 00:07:29.030
"It would be best if I did not.

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:32.199
But, it is a pleasure to make your acquaintance."

00:07:32.199 --> 00:07:37.020
"And you've already met SCP-073, Cain," Dr.
Bright nodded to the man with metal arms.

00:07:37.020 --> 00:07:39.810
"Of course, this little guy needs no introduction."

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:45.570
He patted SCP-999, which wrapped its pseudopods
around his hand and gave it a friendly squeeze.

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:49.509
"I had him with me at Site-17 for some cross-testing
when everything went to hell.

00:07:49.509 --> 00:07:50.710
Good thing, too.

00:07:50.710 --> 00:07:53.500
Never needed an emotional support slime more
in my life."

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:58.060
"Dr. Bright was in a room near mine when the
alarms began to sound," Cain explained.

00:07:58.060 --> 00:08:03.550
"As soon as it became clear something truly
disastrous was happening, we retreated underground

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:06.729
with as many supplies and survivors as we
could."

00:08:06.729 --> 00:08:08.409
"And where were you?"

00:08:08.409 --> 00:08:10.150
The Plague Doctor asked Guy.

00:08:10.150 --> 00:08:11.900
"I was out of town."

00:08:11.900 --> 00:08:13.789
Guy grinned at his own joke.

00:08:13.789 --> 00:08:15.610
"I popped into a forest dimension.

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:17.479
Like the Amazon, but it went on forever.

00:08:17.479 --> 00:08:22.509
It was beautiful, but the mosquitos were the
size of my head, and I couldn't wait to get

00:08:22.509 --> 00:08:23.509
back.

00:08:23.509 --> 00:08:25.470
When I did, though...everyone was gone.

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:28.600
Nothing but the alarm going off over and over
and over again.

00:08:28.600 --> 00:08:33.930
Luckily this guy," he patted Cain on the back,
"found me before those melty things outside

00:08:33.930 --> 00:08:34.930
did."

00:08:34.930 --> 00:08:37.360
"Ah, those who have succumbed to the sun sickness.

00:08:37.360 --> 00:08:38.820
I know them well."

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:40.220
The Plague Doctor's face fell.

00:08:40.220 --> 00:08:43.740
"We lost a member of our party to them not
very long ago."

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.790
"I'm sorry for your loss," Cain said, and
his face made it clear that he really meant

00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:49.790
it.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:50.830
"We have supplies, if you need them."

00:08:50.830 --> 00:08:52.930
He pulled a small cart from the tunnel.

00:08:52.930 --> 00:08:55.760
"Generators, food, clean water, weapons.

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:58.589
We're happy to share in exchange for shelter
here."

00:08:58.589 --> 00:09:00.630
"I thought we agreed I was the leader?"

00:09:00.630 --> 00:09:01.820
Dr. Bright piped up.

00:09:01.820 --> 00:09:07.350
"There are no leaders in a time like this,
only survivors," Cain said solemnly.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:09.880
"But you got to walk at the front."

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:10.880
Dr. Bright pouted.

00:09:10.880 --> 00:09:11.880
"Thank you.

00:09:11.880 --> 00:09:12.980
All of you."

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:16.480
The Plague Doctor's heart swelled with gratitude
at the gesture, at the knowledge that there

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:18.950
were still allies in this nightmarish world.

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.200
"Doctor, are we having company?"

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:22.740
Lord Blackwood awoke behind him.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:25.040
"Yes, my friend, it appears we are."

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:30.340
The next few weeks passed comfortably, almost
joyfully, a far cry from the gray fog of sadness

00:09:30.340 --> 00:09:33.480
that had lingered in the aftermath of Fernand's
passing.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:39.750
SCP-999, Guy, Cain, and Dr. Bright brought
new life into the facility, lighting it up

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:44.100
both figuratively and literally, with the
help of the generators they had brought.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:48.740
Dr. Bright had plans to set up additional
power sources, and devoted his time to experimenting

00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:52.260
with anomalous materials he had managed to
recover from storage.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:56.191
He also offered his services to the Plague
Doctor as a new assistant, someone to help

00:09:56.191 --> 00:10:00.080
him find a cure for the plague that raged
on outside their walls.

00:10:00.080 --> 00:10:04.490
Cain promised to make supply runs, insisting
that his metal limbs made him less vulnerable

00:10:04.490 --> 00:10:06.610
to the effects of the deadly light's beams.

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:10.790
He still covered his skin with the thick robes
whenever he went outside, however.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:15.019
"I'm not sure if it would take me or not,
but that's not a chance I'm willing to take,"

00:10:15.019 --> 00:10:16.820
He had said.

00:10:16.820 --> 00:10:21.420
Meanwhile, Guy entertained the group by reciting
the plots of his favorite movies, tv shows,

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:22.480
and comics.

00:10:22.480 --> 00:10:26.370
He had joined Lord Blackwood as one of the
de facto storytellers of their new little

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:27.910
band of survivors.

00:10:27.910 --> 00:10:32.860
Perhaps, the Plague Doctor thought, they would
find some kind of happiness here.

00:10:32.860 --> 00:10:35.480
Perhaps things really would be alright after
all.

00:10:35.480 --> 00:10:41.140
Meanwhile, out in the nightmarescape beneath
the transformed sun, a wicked mask was wandering

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:43.730
the land in search of a new host.

00:10:43.730 --> 00:10:48.790
Its artificial body had begun to corrode,
to rust and decay beneath the torrent of black

00:10:48.790 --> 00:10:51.690
sludge always pouring from its mouth and eyes.

00:10:51.690 --> 00:10:56.860
Soon, it would not be able to pilot the structure
anymore, and would find itself trapped again,

00:10:56.860 --> 00:11:00.630
waiting for an unsuspecting person to come
along and put it on.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:05.139
In the current climate, the odds of a human
happening upon the mask were lower than ever,

00:11:05.139 --> 00:11:09.260
and, though it would never admit this out
loud, the mask was beginning to get a little

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:10.880
bit nervous.

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:15.000
Perhaps it should head back to the Site, try
to make nice with the Plague Doctor, and see

00:11:15.000 --> 00:11:17.130
if he would offer some assistance...?

00:11:17.130 --> 00:11:19.410
No, that would be pathetic.

00:11:19.410 --> 00:11:22.500
Seeking help from someone so low, so wretched.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:25.209
It would manage fine all on its own.

00:11:25.209 --> 00:11:29.990
Still, as its rickety mannequin legs creaked,
cracking and splitting apart with every step,

00:11:29.990 --> 00:11:34.300
the mask knew it had to move fast, and think
even faster.

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:37.520
If only it could find a weapon, some kind
of leverage.

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:41.740
It could return to the Site and force the
Doctor to become its next host.

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:47.000
As the mask pondered its options, its gaze
fell on one of the fleshy beasts, oozing across

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:50.700
the ground in search of more people to pull
into its molten embrace.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:55.200
The creatures ignored the mask for the most
part, knowing it was inorganic and impossible

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:56.200
to convert.

00:11:56.200 --> 00:12:00.610
But, the mask suddenly thought, could it perhaps
convert one of them?

00:12:00.610 --> 00:12:04.880
Would its consciousness be strong enough to
override the hive mind the monsters all seemed

00:12:04.880 --> 00:12:05.940
to share?

00:12:05.940 --> 00:12:09.940
The mask had overcome the will of kings, of
heroes and villains alike.

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:13.110
Surely it could take on one of these simple
lumps of goo.

00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:15.673
The flesh creature moved slowly, a little
bit at a time.

00:12:15.673 --> 00:12:19.270
It had all the time in the world, the mask
supposed.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:22.040
Or at least, it believed it did.

00:12:22.040 --> 00:12:27.510
As the mask snuck up behind the creature,
its expression changed from a frown to a nasty

00:12:27.510 --> 00:12:28.510
smile.

00:12:28.510 --> 00:12:31.010
It reached up toward itself, angling just
right.

00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:36.100
It would have to land perfectly for this to
work, but it knew it could stick the landing.

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.160
Anywhere on the thing should work.

00:12:38.160 --> 00:12:40.630
After all, it didn't have a face.

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:45.860
For this particular beast, time had run out,
and it was time for the mask to take its body

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:47.339
for a spin.

00:12:47.339 --> 00:12:51.690
Then, it would pay a visit to its old nemesis...

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:55.880
Back at the Site, the Plague Doctor was having
an intense discussion with Dr. Bright about

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:58.639
all that each man had witnessed so far.

00:12:58.639 --> 00:13:02.630
Dr. Bright listened with fascination as the
Plague Doctor described his attempt to treat

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:07.190
one of the infected humans, the invasion of
the massive flesh beast that had taken the

00:13:07.190 --> 00:13:12.570
human survivors right before his eyes, and
Fernand's noble sacrifice to save their shelter

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:13.570
from destruction.

00:13:13.570 --> 00:13:18.750
Dr. Bright, in turn, told of his own trials:
the difficulty getting into the tunnels, the

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:23.490
retrieval of Guy before he was lured outside
by the creatures, and his mission to rescue

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:28.370
as much research as possible before setting
out to find a safe place to hide.

00:13:28.370 --> 00:13:32.839
Sadly, it seemed that the SCP Foundation knew
even less about how to counter the effects

00:13:32.839 --> 00:13:35.089
of the sun than the Plague Doctor did.

00:13:35.089 --> 00:13:40.690
Still, two heads were always better than one,
and an extra set of hands to help with the

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:42.890
work would certainly speed the process along.

00:13:42.890 --> 00:13:47.699
For the first time since Fernand was lost,
the Doctor felt some kind of hope.

00:13:47.699 --> 00:13:53.639
"All we need to do now," the Plague Doctor
said, "is procure another test subject.

00:13:53.639 --> 00:13:58.639
This will, of course, be rather difficult,
as it is perilous to venture outside.

00:13:58.639 --> 00:14:01.970
Perhaps we could appoint some manner of...task
force?"

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:03.290
Dr. Bright nodded.

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:04.770
"We could try that.

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:08.149
Cain's done pretty well going out there so
far, maybe he can bring us back something

00:14:08.149 --> 00:14:10.170
next time he goes out for supplies?"

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:14.540
The Plague Doctor opened his mouth to agree,
but before he could say another word, he heard

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:17.149
something knocking against the window.

00:14:17.149 --> 00:14:21.310
This particular window had been treated to
filter out the deadly light some time ago,

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:25.930
seemingly by accident, when the Foundation
was making the glass resistant to other forms

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:26.930
of attack.

00:14:26.930 --> 00:14:32.040
Through its tinted glass, the Doctor could
make out a strikingly familiar face: the porcelain

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:36.620
mask with the permanent smile, staring in
at him.

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:37.699
"Hello, Doctor."

00:14:37.699 --> 00:14:42.060
The mask laughed, black slime pouring from
its mouth with a gurgling sound.

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:43.060
"Villain!"

00:14:43.060 --> 00:14:44.060
The Plague Doctor spat.

00:14:44.060 --> 00:14:45.570
"What do you want from me?"

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:49.139
"Why must you assume I want something from
you?

00:14:49.139 --> 00:14:52.110
Perhaps I've just come by to pay you a friendly
visit."

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:54.279
The mask's voice was smug, gloating.

00:14:54.279 --> 00:14:57.449
"Because you, sir, are no friend of mine."

00:14:57.449 --> 00:14:59.930
The Plague Doctor crossed his arms defensively.

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:02.290
"Oh, you have guests, I see!

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.690
Dr. Bright, I'm surprised you made it this
far."

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:07.970
The Mask cackled at the sight of the man.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:09.310
"Should have known you'd make it.

00:15:09.310 --> 00:15:12.959
I've heard cockroaches can survive anything,"
Dr. Bright shot back.

00:15:12.959 --> 00:15:15.500
"Have you come here to trade verbal blows?"

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:16.500
The Plague Doctor asked.

00:15:16.500 --> 00:15:18.610
"Or with a true purpose in mind?"

00:15:18.610 --> 00:15:22.380
"Why, Doctor, I came here to visit you.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:25.600
And to show you something wonderful."

00:15:25.600 --> 00:15:29.420
Though it was impossible, the mask's grin
seemed to widen.

00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:32.389
"What could you possibly have to show me?"

00:15:32.389 --> 00:15:36.019
The Plague Doctor was growing irritated, tired
of the mask's games.

00:15:36.019 --> 00:15:37.600
"My new body, of course.

00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:40.899
Silly me, you can't see it when I stand this
close.

00:15:40.899 --> 00:15:44.290
Let me just back away and give you a better
look..."

00:15:44.290 --> 00:15:48.430
With a horrible squelching sound, the mask's
face retreated from the window.

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:52.230
Before the doctors could even stop to ask
one another what it might be, the terrifying

00:15:52.230 --> 00:15:54.770
answer was right in front of their faces.

00:15:54.770 --> 00:16:00.060
The mask was not piloting an ordinary bipedal
host, but rather had positioned itself somehow

00:16:00.060 --> 00:16:03.470
on the top of a massive mound of gelatinous
flesh.

00:16:03.470 --> 00:16:07.800
It was one of the enormous beasts that had
previously tried to invade through the tunnel,

00:16:07.800 --> 00:16:13.140
the amalgamation of dozens of melted people,
stuck together into a roving ball of molten

00:16:13.140 --> 00:16:14.990
skin, bone, and muscle.

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:16.820
"Do you like it?"

00:16:16.820 --> 00:16:18.079
The mask asked.

00:16:18.079 --> 00:16:20.220
"I've been building it for days.

00:16:20.220 --> 00:16:25.850
It started small, you see, just one person-
though I could scarcely call it one anymore.

00:16:25.850 --> 00:16:27.540
So warped and pathetic.

00:16:27.540 --> 00:16:28.540
Sad.

00:16:28.540 --> 00:16:30.480
I could just cry."

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:35.339
The mask flickered to a frowning face, just
for a moment, and then the smile was back.

00:16:35.339 --> 00:16:36.819
"But I won't.

00:16:36.819 --> 00:16:42.000
It was so easy to drop myself right onto the
thing, and before I knew it I had a lovely

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:49.620
new vessel, so malleable, so indestructible,
and so very easy to expand.

00:16:49.620 --> 00:16:51.100
So simple to just..."

00:16:51.100 --> 00:16:53.060
It flexed one of its tentacles here.

00:16:53.060 --> 00:16:59.120
"Snatch up anything I see, pull it out into
the light, and let it become a part of me.

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:01.550
Not that anything has a choice."

00:17:01.550 --> 00:17:03.040
"You're a monster!"

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:04.530
Dr. Bright exclaimed.

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:06.690
"Yes, isn't it marvelous?"

00:17:06.690 --> 00:17:10.220
The mask tossed its head back with a cackle.

00:17:10.220 --> 00:17:14.079
"And I haven't even told you the best part
yet.

00:17:14.079 --> 00:17:16.200
I'm not finished growing, you see.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:23.049
I need more, always more...and you two, and
whatever sad, silly little creatures you have

00:17:23.049 --> 00:17:26.160
in there with you, will make the perfect addition.

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:31.929
I've been waiting for the opportune moment,
and I think now is a perfect time, don't you

00:17:31.929 --> 00:17:32.929
agree?"

00:17:32.929 --> 00:17:34.390
"You'll be waiting a long time."

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:35.390
Dr. Bright said.

00:17:35.390 --> 00:17:37.600
"We will never go outside, devil!"

00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:38.730
The Plague Doctor added.

00:17:38.730 --> 00:17:41.280
"That is perfectly fine, gentleman.

00:17:41.280 --> 00:17:42.390
Perfectly fine.

00:17:42.390 --> 00:17:44.680
I'll just come to you."

00:17:44.680 --> 00:17:48.530
The mask leaned back, and, with all of its
might, threw its massive body against the

00:17:48.530 --> 00:17:50.010
wall with a crash.

00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:53.110
The building shook with the impact, rattling
from the blow.

00:17:53.110 --> 00:17:54.630
"Can it break through?"

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:56.080
Dr. Bright asked, wide-eyed.

00:17:56.080 --> 00:18:00.080
"I'm afraid I cannot say for certain," The
Plague Doctor said solemnly.

00:18:00.080 --> 00:18:04.539
"These monsters...they are unlike anything
I have ever studied before."

00:18:04.539 --> 00:18:06.680
"Same," Dr. Bright grimaced.

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:09.610
All the while, the mask continued its assault
on their hiding place.

00:18:09.610 --> 00:18:14.039
As it collided with the wall again and again,
the two doctors heard a sound that made their

00:18:14.039 --> 00:18:17.580
stomachs drop: the sound of something splintering
apart.

00:18:17.580 --> 00:18:18.710
It was working.

00:18:18.710 --> 00:18:21.370
The wall was beginning to give way.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:22.370
"Dr. Bright!"

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:23.370
The Plague Doctor cried.

00:18:23.370 --> 00:18:24.370
"We must retreat.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.830
Do you know of a safe place to which we can
flee?"

00:18:26.830 --> 00:18:28.990
"I think I just might."

00:18:28.990 --> 00:18:30.059
Dr. Bright nodded.

00:18:30.059 --> 00:18:31.570
"Quickly, gather the others!

00:18:31.570 --> 00:18:33.330
We have no time to waste!"

00:18:33.330 --> 00:18:37.520
Dr. Bright and the Plague Doctor assembled
the rest of their ragtag group: Cain was engaged

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:43.789
in a lengthy conversation with Guy while SCP-999
played with a wind-up toy car it had found.

00:18:43.789 --> 00:18:47.240
Lord Blackwood was brewing another batch of
his unusual ale.

00:18:47.240 --> 00:18:51.620
They were all shocked at the news of the sudden
invasion, but as fast as they could, they

00:18:51.620 --> 00:18:55.650
gathered their supplies, a few weapons, and
the remaining generators.

00:18:55.650 --> 00:19:01.180
Then, they headed back into the tunnels, but
not before Cain made one final defensive move.

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:06.260
Using his anomalous strength, he dragged an
enormous steel cabinet in front of the entrance,

00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:07.270
blocking it from view.

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:12.820
If the mask did break in, hopefully, it would
not be able to see where they had gone.

00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:17.780
Then, together, they left the little slice
of familiarity they had carved out in this

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:21.630
frightening new world and set off into the
unknown.

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:29.159
Now go check out “When Day Breaks SCP-049”
and “SCP-001 - Can SCP-049 Finally Cure

00:19:29.159 --> 00:19:30.410
When Day Breaks?”

00:19:30.410 --> 00:19:32.130
for the first two parts of this epic tale!

